 "strategy": {
  "summary": "Buy Treasury futures on the last few trading days of each month, day session only. Hartley & Schwarz (Federal Reserve) find coupon Treasuries earn positive, significant returns only over the month's last few days (Sharpe about 1, 1990\u20132018), driven by index funds and other benchmarked holders buying at the month-end index rebalance (the \"strike\"). Their numbers are close-to-close, overnight included; this run keeps only the 08:00\u201317:00 ET part, because nothing is held overnight.",
  "formula": "Long on each of the month's last N trading days, from the entry time to the exit time",
  "rules": [
   {
    "label": "Days",
    "text": "Each of the last 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 or 6 NYSE trading days of the calendar month, each its own trade. Optional filters: skip scheduled FOMC statement days; also skip days with a Treasury note or bond auction."
   },
   {
    "label": "Enter",
    "text": "Buy at 08:20, 09:00, 10:00, 11:00, 12:00 or 14:00 ET, at that minute's open. The day is skipped if the bars have a gap of more than 5 minutes there."
   },
   {
    "label": "Exit",
    "text": "Sell at 15:00 ET (CBOT settlement), 16:00 ET, or at the index strike: 15:00 ET on month-ends before 14 Jan 2021 and 16:00 ET after, when Bloomberg moved its Treasury index pricing time. On early-close days the trade closes at the last bar. Optional stop 0.25% or 0.5% below the entry price, live during the trade."
   },
   {
    "label": "Size",
    "text": "One position at a time, never held overnight. As many whole ZN contracts as the account covers at full contract value (no leverage), starting from $1,000,000."
   }
  ],
  "axes": [
   {
    "label": "Bar size",
