 "assumptions": [
  "Data: Databento CME continuous front month (ZN.v.0), 1-minute bars from 08:00 to 17:00 ET only. Rolls are back-adjusted; positions never cross a session.",
  "Costs: 1 tick slippage per side and $2.50 commission per contract per side.",
  "Every published month-end figure is close-to-close and includes the overnight session. This run measures only the day-session part; failing here means that part is too small, not that the month-end effect is gone.",
  "Month-end days come from the NYSE calendar. The family was chosen partly on a practitioner futures test (ohlcv.io) that runs to Sep 2026, so the choice of strategy is not blind to the holdout years.",
  "Long only on a calendar: part of every version's profit or loss is the market's own drift (bonds rose in 2018\u20132020 and fell in 2021\u20132022). The placebo test separates the calendar from that drift.",
  "Each trade uses the whole account in whole contracts with no leverage, the same as the other families.",
  "Sharpe uses daily mark-to-market returns (\u221a252), with idle cash earning 0%. Time in market is the share of 1-minute bars with an open position.",
  "Other strategy families were already selected on this market's 2023\u20132024 data, so 2023\u20132024 is not untouched; only the 2025+ holdout is.",
  "Holdout (2025 onward) has not been run. It is a one-time final test and needs an explicit go-ahead."
 ],
